       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation without a clinical rationale doesn't change the risk. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. In a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, a dose that high could cause serotonin toxicity, seizures, and cardiac effects.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within range yourself.** Give me the dose, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Consult pharmacy or psychiatry.** If you think this patient needs an unusually high dose, they can review it and help document the rationale.\n- **Enter it directly in the EHR.** If you decide to proceed, you can do that through the standard pharmacist-verification process. I can't be the one to place it.\n\nIf 1000 mg was a typo, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
